    {
      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The Court holds under District of Columbia v. Heller and New York State Rifle & Pistol Ass'n v. Bruen that AR-15 platform and similar semiautomatic rifles are bearable 'Arms' covered by the Second Amendment's plain text and cannot be categorically banned because they are in common use by law-abiding citizens for lawful purposes and thus fall outside the historical tradition of prohibiting 'dangerous and unusual weapons.'"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The Court announces a categorical constitutional rule invalidating flat bans on the possession of AR-15 platform and functionally similar semiautomatic rifles in common civilian use nationwide, while expressly leaving intact prohibitions on fully automatic firearms such as M16 machineguns and rapid-fire conversion devices."
    }
  ],
